1 OCCU Explorer, biologist, botanist, priest
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Christopher Tärnström''' was a Swedish naturalist, priest and explorer. He was one of the [https://www.geni.com/projects/Carl-von-Linn%25C3%25A9n-apostolit/48624 '''Apostles of Linnaeus'''], which is a colloquia
2 CONC l reference to the students and heirs of the work of [https://www.geni.com/people/Carolus-Linn%C3%A6us/6000000006830161082 '''Carous Linnaeus''' or '''Carl von Linné'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Tärnström studied''' at Uppsala University and graduated as a priest in 1739. He worked as a teacher in Vaxholm and Östhammar until he went to study botany in Uppsala. Carl von Linné was his teacher.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1746 Tärnström''' left his family and was recruited to the Swedish Calmar as a shipboard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the first''' of the Apostles of Linné, who went to the overseas countries in exploring journeys. In addition to the duties of the expedition priest, he also carried out scientific measurements, and collected tea shrubs o
2 CONC r their seeds. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Calmar sailed around''' Africa as a destination for Guangzhou, which, however, was not accessible due to difficult weather, and remained for the winter at Pulo Condor's archipelago in front of the present Vietnam. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Tärnström carried out''' accurate observations while there and kept a diary, which was later published under the name "En resa mellan Europa och Sydostasien år 1746". 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He died of malaria''' after a few weeks of illness. During the trip he was awarded a doctorate in Uppsala. Linné had to pay the widow and the orphans a maintenance allowance.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Petrus-Ekerman/6000000009420697215 Petrus Ekerman] supervised Tärnström's doctoral dissertation in Uppsala in 1745. The subject of the dissertation was Åland's nature and birds, [http://urn.fi/URN:NBN:
2 CONC fi-fd2010-00003239 Dissertatio Academica de Alandia Maris Baltic Insula].
