1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  William W Von Christierson graduated from the U.S. Naval Academy in 1951 and first served aboard the USS Toledo (CA-133).  He reported to Submarine School, New London in 1952.  His submarine service prior to comma
2 CONC nding the Cusk was aboard the USS Baya (AGSS-318), USS Pickerel (SS-524), Staff, U.S. Submarine Base Pearl Harbor, Executive Officer of the USS Bream (SS-243), and Staff Commander Hawaiian Sea Frontier.  He relieved as Commanding 
2 CONC Officer of the USS Cusk on 23 May 1964.  He was the 12th Commanding Officer of the Cusk and was well loved and respected by the crew.  He commanded the Cusk until 5 June 1966.
