1 NOTE {geni:about_me} One of the 1.2 million Swedes that came to America in the 19th Century. Born an illegitimate child in Hova Parish in Västra Götaland, Sweden. She worked as a maid when she was young. Left for America May 15 1888 an
2 CONC d arrived three days later May 18 1888 in New York. When Kristina came to America she angelized her name to Christine. She met Charles Johnson and married him November 3rd 1892 in Sioux City, Des Moines, Iowa, USA or Moline, Illin
2 CONC ois. They moved to Moline, Illinois where both her kids were born. Then they moved to Des Moines Iowa where they lived for several years. Moved to Los Angeles, CA after her husband died with her daughter Mildred. She died there Oc
2 CONC tober 9th, 1949. She was taken back to Des Moines, IA and buried next to her husband on the 12th.
2 CONT
